{
  "task_id": "d01",
  "request_sha256": "e15b8a017f08e0a8057084fca2c348f199b176a67903807488142e56483f3b84",
  "proof": "by\n  intro G H g h f hf a b c d ha hb hc hd\n  simp only [hf, ha, hb, hc, hd, h.one_mul]\n",
  "bridge": "This baseline proof uses only the supplied foundation and no candidate package. The raw multiplication-preservation hypothesis hf expands the image of the balanced product into the corresponding three multiplications in H. The four kernel hypotheses replace f a, f b, f c, and f d by h.one. The group law h.one_mul then reduces all three products to h.one, which is the original goal. No representation bridge is needed. Packaging is not Lean verification."
}

