{
  "task_id": "d02",
  "request_sha256": "8faa7090ed5c56a85e39289262e9059617bccdc5a0ea40a8cd17ddab6b197c06",
  "proof": "by\n  intro G H g h f hf op hop x y z hx hy hz\n  rw [hop, hop, hf, hf, hx, hy, hz, h.one_mul, h.one_mul]\n",
  "bridge": "This baseline has no candidate package, so the proof works directly in the supplied vocabulary. The two instances of hop identify op (op x y) z with g.mul z (g.mul y x). The two instances of hf transport this product to h.mul (f z) (h.mul (f y) (f x)). The original hypotheses hx, hy and hz replace all three images with h.one; the foundation axiom h.one_mul then reduces both products to h.one. No representation bridge or candidate lemma is used. Packaging is not Lean verification; this is a supplied proof awaiting the controller's check."
}

