  "proof": "by\n  intro G H g h f hf x y z hxy\n  rw [hf x z, hf y z, hxy]\n",
  "bridge": "This is the baseline condition, so no candidate package or representation bridge is used. Rewrite f (g.mul x z) and f (g.mul y z) using the supplied multiplication-preservation hypothesis hf. The hypothesis f x = f y then identifies the resulting expressions h.mul (f x) (f z) and h.mul (f y) (f z), making both sides of the required equivalence identical."
}

