{
  "task_id": "d07",
  "request_sha256": "b9811903e0cf40984556e30fd118350b406705a813d59cf30a5291555dbabd46",
  "proof": "by\n  intro G H g h f hf\n  refine ⟨fun x y => ⟨g.mul x.val y.val, ?_⟩, ?_⟩\n  · rw [hf, x.property, y.property, h.one_mul]\n  · intro x y\n    rfl\n",
  "bridge": "This is the baseline condition, with no candidate package available. The goal is to equip the subtype of elements mapped by f to h.one with a multiplication whose underlying value is g.mul. Define the operation on subtype elements x and y using g.mul x.val y.val. Its membership proof uses hf to rewrite the image of that product, then the subtype proofs x.property and y.property to replace both images by h.one; h.one_mul finishes closure. The required equality of underlying values is definitional, so rfl closes it. Packaging this term does not constitute Lean verification."
}

