  "proof": "by\n  intro G H g h f hf s hs x y\n  refine ⟨g.mul (s x) (s y), ?_, rfl⟩\n  rw [hf, hs x, hs y]\n",
  "bridge": "This is the baseline condition, so no candidate definitions or lemmas are used. Choose z = g.mul (s x) (s y). The supplied multiplication-preservation hypothesis hf identifies f z with h.mul (f (s x)) (f (s y)); the section equations hs x and hs y then rewrite this to h.mul x y. The requested identity for z holds by reflexivity. Packaging has not verified this Lean term."
}

