  "proof": "by\n  intro I G H g h f hf x y hx hy i\n  calc\n    f i (g.mul x y) = h.mul (f i x) (f i y) := hf i x y\n    _ = h.mul h.one h.one := by rw [hx i, hy i]\n    _ = h.one := h.one_mul h.one\n",
  "bridge": "This is the baseline condition, so no candidate definitions or properties are available. For each index i, the supplied hypothesis hf i x y transports multiplication through f i. The raw hypotheses hx i and hy i identify both factors with h.one. The supplied group law h.one_mul h.one then returns the result to the original indexed kernel-closure goal. No additional representation bridge is needed."
}

