  "proof": "by\n  intro G H g h f hf a x y hxy\n  simp only [hf, hxy]\n",
  "bridge": "This is the baseline condition, so no candidate definitions or properties are used. The original goal compares the images of two conjugation expressions. Applying the raw multiplicativity hypothesis hf to the outer and inner products expresses each image using h.mul, f a, f x or f y, and f (g.inv a). The supplied equality f x = f y then rewrites those expressions to the same term. No group laws beyond the supplied multiplicativity hypothesis are needed."
}

